  "query_preview": "/THURSDAY THROUGH SUNDAY/... \nForecast concern is increasing for the potential of tropical \nmoisture surging northward into the region as early as Thursday \nnight into Friday, but more so for the coming weekend. NHC shows a\ntropical disturbance currently near 10N and 107W with a 90% \nchance of cyclone formation this week and likely tracking \nnorthward off the coast of Baja by Friday into the weekend. There \nis still a lot of uncertainty with this potential tropical \nsystem, but model guidance has been coming to a bit better \nconsensus the last several model runs. Roughly 90% of the GEFS and\nEPS members now show PWATs increasing to 1.8-2.2\" over portions of \nour area by Friday or Saturday. Given this likely increase in \nmoisture, PoPs have gone up starting Friday and continue through \nthe weekend. It will likely be at least 2 or 3 more days until we \nhave a good idea on what would likely happen late this week. \nGetting tropical moisture into our region is definitely not \nunusual, but many times when it happens we struggle to build \ninstability due to extensive cloudiness and poor lapse rates. \nHowever, it seems quite likely a Pacific trough will be situated \nalong or just off the West Coast which may provide for enough \nupper level forced ascent to overcome the likely lackluster \ninstability. We will continue to watch this throughout the week as\nit very well could lead to another round of heavy rainfall at \nsome point.",
